Description: the table of named groups of a compiled pattern initialised after its allocation: add_name() compares the names of its entries past their ends, so a pattern with named groups whose names begin alike, (?<f>)(?<fir>), read uninitialised memory while it was compiled (MemorySanitizer, Exim bug 2661); there is no release of PCRE1 after 8.45
Origin: Petr Pisar's fix as Fedora carries it on 8.45 (pcre-8.44-Inicialize-name-table-memory-region.patch, f0bb9e8b of 19.10.2020), the same as files/patch-name-table of devel/pcre of azsupport/ports

--- a/ext/pcre/pcrelib/pcre_compile.c
+++ b/ext/pcre/pcrelib/pcre_compile.c
@@ -9423,6 +9423,11 @@
   goto PCRE_EARLY_ERROR_RETURN;
   }
 
+/* Initialize the memory. Name table entry values are accessed past their ends
+ * (e.g. in add_name()) when comparing the values. Also a size of the entry can
+ * grow later. It's safer to initialize here than to hunt the gaps later. */
+memset(re, 0, size);
+
